From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ophuscado <postbox@ophuscado.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 17:54:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 03/10] thunderbolt: Take the subsystem from asahi-wip-7.2 for
 Apple USB4

The stock Asahi 7.1 tree has no USB4 host driver for Apple Silicon. The
driver (drivers/thunderbolt/apple.c, Sven Peter) lives in the Asahi 7.2
work-in-progress tree and builds on Thunderbolt core changes made
between 7.1 and 7.2, which split the PCI specifics out of the NHI code
and added the hooks a platform NHI needs. Picking those one by one
conflicts from the first commit on, so drivers/thunderbolt,
include/linux/thunderbolt.h and drivers/net/thunderbolt are taken whole
from branch tbt/pcie of this fork at 523466d61f0b, which is
asahi-wip-7.2 at 236788cd2602 plus the lab's four Thunderbolt commits:

  thunderbolt: apple: Flag 20 Gb/s for cables faster than Gen 3
  DEBUG: thunderbolt: apple: Add cable_info_or parameter
  thunderbolt: Add out-of-band protocol adapter notifications
  thunderbolt: apple: Start the PCIe controller with its tunnel

The one adaptation: 7.2 split mod_devicetable.h into
include/linux/device-id/, so thunderbolt.h includes mod_devicetable.h
here.

Check: full arm64 build of this tree with clang 18, CONFIG_USB4=y and
USB4_APPLE_SOC=m, no errors or warnings. Not run yet.
